  "purpose": "Mirrors the recorded 34-point tau2_retail TEST fork benchmark's SIZE (204 units, same 2 arms x 3 seeds shape) AND its prefix-depth (k) distribution, so a checkpoint chosen on this set is evaluated across the same range of dialogue progress the test set covers, not only on near-fresh prefixes.",
  "defect_this_supersedes": "An earlier version of this file sorted the pool by (task_id, trace_sha, k) and round-robinned by task, which always drew each task's shallowest available point first: k in {2: 18, 4: 16}, median 2, mean 2.94, against the pool's own median 8 / mean 10.67 and the TEST set's median 12.5 / mean 12.32. That sample tested a checkpoint only on prefixes where almost all the work remained. Superseded by the k-stratified rule below.",
  "selection_rule": "Deterministic, reproducible from tau2_retail_dev.pool.json plus the recorded TEST benchmark's own k values alone (no randomness): (1) read the 34 k values of the recorded tau2_retail TEST fork benchmark from runs/*/manifest.json via scripts/run_tau2_forks.py's points_from_runs(suite='tau2_retail', split='test', arms=['inquirer_prompted','self_ask']) -- run_ids_sha 1a060380806fff3e -- giving 34 target k values (histogram in docs/HPC_FORKS.md); (2) sort the 34 targets ascending and draw one pool point per target, in that order; for each target k, use the pool's exact k if any pool point (not already drawn) has it, otherwise the available k closest to the target (ties toward the smaller k) -- the only such case is target k=34, which has no pool point (the pool's own max is 31) and maps to k=31; (3) within a stratum (all draws sharing one resolved k), break ties by task-diversity: prefer the task_id that has contributed the FEWEST points to the sample so far, cumulative across every stratum drawn before it (not reset per stratum), then ascending int(task_id), then ascending trace_sha. tests/test_fork_pool_selection.py re-derives this exact list from the pool file and the live TEST-set manifests and asserts it equals what is stored below.",
